{
  "name": "1940_viipuri",
  "title": "Viipuri Gateway, Feb-Mar 1940 (Winter War)",
  "notes": "The fall of the Mannerheim Line gateway to Viipuri, 11-15 Feb 1940: Timoshenko's North-Western Front concentrated nine rifle divisions + five tank brigades on the 16 km Summa-Lahde-Munasuo sector (7th Army under Meretskov). The main blow fell on Lahde road: Alyabushev's 123rd Rifle Division (245/255/272 RR + 323 AP — Order of Lenin, the only division decorated before the ceasefire) with the 35th Tank Brigade (T-28s + the 112th OTB T-26s, later joined by a KV platoon in March) took the Poppius (Sj4, hill 65.5) and 'Million' bunkers on 11-12 Feb; 100th Rifle Division (355/472/508 RR, 46th Howitzer AR) battered Summa village; 138th Rifle Division (554/650/768 RR, 295 AP, Red Banner) held the Munasuo swamp flank. The worn-down Finnish 3rd Divisioona (Paalu; ex-6.D, renumbered Jan 1940 — JR 6/7/8 ex JR 16/17/18, KTR 3) held the Summa-Lahde line at org 40 after two months of attrition; Isakson's 5th Divisioona (JR 13/14/15, KTR 5) arrived as the 13 Feb counterattack force (with III./JR-67 of the new 23rd Div attached); Mannerheim ordered the II Corps back to the V-Line on 15 Feb. Rosters verified (sources: en.Wikipedia Battle of Summa / 123rd Rifle Division / 138th Rifle Division / Battle of Honkaniemi / 5th Division (Winter War) / 6th Division (Winter War) / Army of the Isthmus; ru.Wikipedia Proryv linii Mannergeima / 100-ya strelkovaya diviziya). Scale = 1939 calibration (same as 1939_warsaw): fresh Soviet divisions at full org 60, exhausted 3.D at 40, the 5.D counterattack force at 48, bunkers at 55 with defense 26; the defender plays tactical_withdrawal into the city while the bay guns watch the SW shore. AXIS (verified in HOI4): dirs=SE — the attacker comes from province 9100, the province SE of Viipuri (9206) on the historical Leningrad-Viipuri road (Summa-Lahde) axis; per-pixel sector origin inference (generator.rs) makes dirs=SE match 9100's southern-half border and clips the staging strip to it, replacing the old NE/Lappeenranta compromise (6082 is actually the province NORTH of 9206). The bay (SW, ocean) and the huge E neighbour 9100's full border remain unusable as axes (stretched band, gap 42).",
